==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*pleḱ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|replyen}}, {{m|enm|replien}}, borrowed from {{der|en|fro|replier||to reply}}, from the {{der|en|la|replico|replicō, replicāre|t=to fold back}} (in Late or Medieval Latin "to reply, repeat"), from {{m|la|re}} + {{m|la|plicō||to fold}}; the noun derives from the verb by [[nominalisation]]. Doublet of {{m|en|replicate}} and {{m|en|replica}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈplaɪ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-reply.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyphenation|en|re|ply}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪ|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{wikidata lexeme|L93}}
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|intransitive}} To give a [[written]] or [[spoken]] [[response]], especially to a [[question]], [[request]], [[accusation]] or [[criticism]]; to [[answer]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=w:San Francisco Chronicle|title=One of San Francisco’s strangest buildings was a mash-up masterpiece|date=March 19 2021|author=Gary Kamiya
|text=When an East Coast industrialist who wanted [Willis] Polk to design a building told the architect that he admired his work, Polk '''replied''', “I would feel complimented if I thought you knew anything about art.”
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260427203232/https://www.sfchronicle.com/vault/portalsofthepast/article/One-of-San-Francisco-s-strangest-buildings-was-16038435.php}}
#: {{lb|en|intransitive}} ''Please '''reply''' to my letter.''
#: {{lb|en|transitive}} ''"Sorry I'm late," '''replied''' the student.''
#: {{lb|en|transitive}} ''He '''replied''' that he was not sure.''
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[act]] or [[gesture]] in response.
#: {{ux|en|Joanne '''replied''' to Pete's insult with a slap to his face.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1988|author=Emmanuel Doe Ziorklui|title=Ghana: Nkrumah to Rawlings|passage=It is a sound to be dreaded until you ascertain that it is being made by friendly forces; even then, your welcome to it must be tempered with some caution, because gunfire usually leads to '''replying''' gunfire{{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Steve Cowens|title=Steel City Rivals
|passage={{...}} [[bulge the onion bag|bulged the onion bag]] for the Blades, and Downes and Prendergast '''replied''' for the Owls.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[repeat]] something back; to [[echo]].

